WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.790
January 3, 2022.

2
00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:07.930
One US dollar buys 115.27 Japanese yen.

3
00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:13.810
By October 20, that same
dollar buys 149.82 yen.

4
00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:16.080
That's about 30 percent more.

5
00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:20.570
All year, the Fed keeps raising its
target for the federal funds rate.

6
00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:23.270
Japan's rate stays below zero.

7
00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:25.850
So how can one decision by a central bank

8
00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:28.990
change what a currency is
worth around the world?

9
00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:31.780
In this mission, you'll
trace who buys dollars,

10
00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:33.180
and who sells them.

11
00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:36.220
Then you'll run up a budget
deficit yourself and follow

12
00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:38.440
it through two linked markets.

13
00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:41.770
Your mission: explain how
one decision by a central

14
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:45.240
bank can change what a currency
is worth around the world.
